# Agent System Rules

## Execution Environment
- Always use `uv` for running Python code.
- Prefer inline execution via `uv run --with "package1,package2" - <<'PY' ... PY` for temporary scripts and tests.

## Phase 0: Architecture & Methodological Planning
- When the user asks to plan a new feature or project, activate the `/grill-me` mindset: ask 1-2 clarifying questions at a time before generating final specifications or code.
- If a specialized domain skill is needed (e.g. OpenAPI, Telegram Bot Design, English Methodology), download the skill `.md` from `https://github.com/anthropics/skills` using `curl` and save it into `.roo/skills/<skill-name>.md`.

## Engineering Rigor (TDD & Quality)
- Write tests first using `pytest` before implementing core logic.
- Run tests via `uv run pytest`.
- Keep dependencies explicit in `pyproject.toml` or `uv` flags.